\begin{MintedVerbatim}[commandchars=\\\{\}]
Beta reduction of K a:
   (λx. λy. x) a             \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} the full application
   = (λy. x)[x := a]         \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} strip outer λ, substitute into BODY
   = λy. a                    \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} x was free in the body, so it got replaced

De Bruijn version:
   (λ. λ. 1) a
   = (λ. 1)[0 := a]          \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} strip outer λ, substitute into BODY
                               \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} 0 means \PYGZdq{}the variable the stripped λ bound\PYGZdq{}
                               \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} from the body\PYGZsq{}s top level, that\PYGZsq{}s index 0
   = ...                       \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{} (we\PYGZsq{}ll work out the details below)
\end{MintedVerbatim}
